segments.text:
proposition 1 BY that precept;
Thou ſhalt not ſteale, the Iſraelites could not be reprooued of theft when they robbed Aegypt:
ſince to vſurpe other mens goods againſt the will of the Lord, belongeth vnto the nature of theft. But they carried not out other mens goods, but their own; to wit, being giuen them by God.
